# Line endings: LF in the repo AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, git stores whatever bytes it is given and checks out `native`,
# which is CRLF on Windows. Since this project is edited from more than one
# place, pinning LF keeps diffs honest instead of full of phantom whole-file
# changes.
#
# Content-neutral when added, verified with `git ls-files --eol`: all 66 tracked
# text files already read i/lf, and the two PNG icons already read i/-text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never let git guess on these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
